// Pixel art as data: one character per pixel, '.' is clear, every other
// character is a palette key. Authored with a scratch generator, then
// committed as plain grids: edit the rows here directly.
//
// Chapter 4-1, Newbury Street at night: Back Bay brownstones, the brick
// sidewalk, gas lamps, warm boutique windows, fire escapes. Same layout as
// the rooftop set so the chunk baker works unchanged: tiles are 16 x 16,
// anchor top left, each kind one anim whose frames are variants (fps 0, pick
// by column hash). roofTop is the brick sidewalk (row 0 its lamp lit
// edge, the pavers edge on) over a granite curb face, then brownstone
// ashlar (variant 1 fallen leaves, variant 2 a cast iron coal hole cover
// with a lamp glint); roofEdgeLeft and roofEdgeRight its rounded ends;
// roofFill the brownstone facade (variant 1 a lit 2 over 2 sash with a
// keystone, variant 2 the lit front of a bow front bay; weight the plain
// wall heaviest); oneWay a fire escape landing (an iron grate with see
// through slats, braces under it); stone a rusticated brownstone block;
// spikes a front garden fence of spear finials on a granite curb (hazard);
// brick a florist's crate of autumn flowers (breakable); auraBlock the
// sigma crate in a granite frame; vent a garden level window behind bars
// (matches roofFill); pipe a copper downspout run sideways (tileable).
// Courses are 8 tall with blocks 16 long, toned by course, so any variants
// sit side by side without a seam.
//
// Decor anchor is the bottom left (y is the top of the floor row it stands
// on). Light sources, in decor pixels from the top left: gasLamp the
// lantern at (8, 9); goalLamp two lanterns at (15, 10) and (27, 10);
// shopWindow the window glow, centre (24, 16), its pendant lamps at (13, 13),
// (25, 13), (37, 13). goalLamp (the goal: the end of the street at the
// garden's edge, a double lantern post, the iron garden fence, a willow):
// 4 frames of the mantles flickering, loop.
//
// awning: the shop awning bounce pad, 32 x 8 (two tiles wide, striped
// fabric, a scalloped valance, iron frame ends). anchor (0, 1): row 1 is
// the fabric's top at rest, so the anchor sits on the cell's top left and
// the rebound frame can bulge up into row 0. idle 1 frame; squash 3 frames
// played once on a bounce (deep sag, rebound bulging up, settle), driven by
// w.bounces[i].t. Draw one awning per pair of bounce cells, or clip a 16 px
// half (the stripes and scallops repeat every 8 px).
//
// NEWBURY_GLOW lists the keys that glow: Q lamp, R mantle core, S lit
// window, T dim window, U shop window, V red, W cool reflection, X deep
// amber, ^ ~ the aura sigma, 7 8 warm halos, * red halo.
//
// NEWBURY_BACKDROP: three 512 px tileable strips for the parallax, bottom on
// the horizon (the bottom row is one colour, so it can be lifted). far
// (112): over the Back Bay roofs, the boxy tower with its lit crown band and
// mast (red light) and the tall mirror glass slab taking the sky, notched
// at its ends, its edge catching the crown's light; a campanile with a lit
// belfry; sodium haze. mid (80): brownstone and red brick row houses, bow
// fronts over three floors, mansards with lit dormers, cornices, chimneys,
// stoops, garden level shops lit or dark. near (64): street trees with lamp
// light on their undersides, gas lamps with halos, a low iron fence, parked
// cars, the brick sidewalk with light pooled under each lamp.
